comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-01T11:19:35.934Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate-check evidence: the strict duplicate guard flagged pm-gh1605 (closed). Its title, AC and resolution are scoped to pm history only ('Preserve newest compact/provenance history...'), so reopening it would widen a shipped item. This item covers the sibling annotation readers that did not receive the same tail-preserving default. Related closed precedent: pm-6vfg (MCP pm_comments default limit). Searched: pm search 'comments default page oldest latest bounded read'."
  "2026-11-07T22:53:39.958Z","harness:claude-code","Investigation and implementation (2026-11-07, branch fix/annotation-collection-reads). Root cause: the universal budget compaction (compactRowsToBudget in src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts) and the --output-limit bound (boundReadOutputRows in src/sdk/read-output-rows.ts) always retained the FIRST rows of a declared collection, while the annotation producer stores entries oldest first. So pm comments pm-7zs0 --json returned indexes 1..28 of 263, and --output-limit 2 returned the two oldest comments while --limit 2 returned the two newest. pm learnings was not a read-output surface at all, so its reads had no output ceiling.\n\nFix: PM_READ_OUTPUT_TAIL_RETENTION_POLICIES (src/sdk/read-output/continuation.ts) declares comments, notes and learnings as newest-tail paths, as data. Budget compaction and --output-limit retain the tail of those paths. Their continuation cursor carries direction backward: offset counts the older rows still withheld, and replay slices [0, offset) then keeps that slice's newest rows. A cursor whose direction disagrees with the path's declared retention is refused as read_output_cursor_stale. A withheld tail sets total_count beside count, and a producer returned_count is refreshed to the delivered page. learnings joined PM_READ_OUTPUT_SURFACES with --limit as its legacy amount alias.\n\nMeasured on this tracker with the built CLI: bare pm comments pm-7zs0 --json now returns indexes 238..263 (count 26, total_count 263), the cursor's next page returns 211..237, and --output-limit 2 returns 262 and 263.\n"
  "2026-11-08T00:52:17.967Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 1 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) on PR 1685 found three issues, all verified and fixed. (P1) Adding learnings as a read-output surface without listing its mutation keys in HYBRID_READ_MUTATION_KEYS admitted pm learnings --add/--edit/--delete combined with universal output controls. Before the fix, pm learnings <id> --add x --output-budget 500 wrote the entry (exit 0), and with a stale --output-cursor the write would land before the cursor refusal. learnings now lists add, stdin, file, edit and delete, so the combination is refused before dispatch (exit 2). (P2) attachTailRetentionTotal overwrote a producer total_count with the continuation total. That total describes only the producer's own page (MCP lists 20 comments by default), so a 60-comment item reported total_count 20. An existing producer total is now kept. (P2) A backward replay that needs no further compaction kept the producer count (40 instead of the 26 delivered rows). applyReadOutputContinuation now sets count and returned_count to the delivered slice. Three regression specs in tests/unit/sdk/read-output/tail-retention.spec.ts fail with the two fixed files stashed and pass with them.\n"
  "2026-11-08T01:03:47.180Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) confirmed the round-1 fixes and found one more reachable P2, verified and fixed. Positional annotation text is a mutation that the read-output guard never saw, because it is not an option key. pm learnings <id> \"text\" --output-budget 1 appended the entry and then failed the output budget (exit 2), and a retry with the suggested budget appended again. The same bypass existed before this PR for pm comments and pm notes. The preAction validation in src/cli/main.ts now passes annotationPositionalMutationOptions (src/cli/register-annotations.ts), which exposes the text slot of comments, notes and learnings as add. Positional text combined with a universal output control is refused before dispatch for all three commands, through the pm item spelling and the --id form. Reads with an output budget and positional appends without controls are unchanged. tests/unit/cli/annotation-positional-output-controls.spec.ts fails for all three commands with the main.ts wiring stashed.\n"
  "2026-11-08T01:28:51.818Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 4 (gpt-6.1-sol, xhigh) confirmed the round 1-3 and CodeRabbit fixes. It reported that pm learnings <id> --text x --output-budget 1 still writes, because the guard did not list the text alias. Through the shipped CLI this does not reproduce: argv canonicalization rewrites --text to --add before Commander parses (normalized_args shows --add), the guard refuses the command with exit 2, and nothing is written. The same holds for comments --text/--comment/--body and notes --text/--note. Codex's in-memory reproduction drove Commander directly and skipped that layer. As defense in depth, HYBRID_READ_MUTATION_KEYS now also lists each command's text aliases (comment, text, note, learning). The guard therefore holds for any caller whose argv was not canonicalized, and the tail-retention spec asserts each alias.\n"
  "2026-11-08T02:51:55.785Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit full review of the final head (9 threads). Fixed for this item: (1) The read-output surface contract still declared budget_retention_policy ordered_prefix for comments, notes and learnings. They now declare ordered_suffix, derived from the same tail-retention declaration so the two cannot drift. (2) A backward replay page now reports total_count: a producer total is kept, otherwise the cursor's snapshot total is used. (3) notes structured_event_count is documented as the structured events in the returned projection. It is now declared as a delivered-row counter on the notes tail policy and recounted after --output-limit, budget compaction and backward replay. (4) A built-CLI regression spec (tests/integration/read-output/annotation-tail-retention.integration.spec.ts) bounds bare comments, notes and learnings reads of 40 entries in JSON and TOON. It asserts that the newest entry, total_count 40 and a backward cursor are delivered, and that the older page follows. The tail policy moved to the dependency-free module src/sdk/read-output/tail-retention.ts, because the surface contracts read it while their own module initializes. The census link in DIAGNOSTIC_OUTPUT_CONTRACTS.md is labelled as current-main evidence, with a pointer to the release tag.\n"
  "2026-11-08T03:06:24.176Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review of the round-3 commit found one P2, verified and fixed. The structured_event_count recount read the delivered rows after field projection. So applyReadOutputDimensions on notes with outputInclude index,data and outputLimit 1 kept the JSON event but reported structured_event_count 0, because the projection had dropped format; budget pages and backward replays did the same. The unprojected producer result now travels on the continuation state. refreshReadOutputDeliveredRowCounters counts the producer rows that match the delivered newest tail, which ends at the pre-budget row count (the whole collection, or the older slice a backward cursor replays). The recount runs once after projection, the amount bound and replay, and again inside budget compaction. A regression spec covers the projected limit, budget and replay cases, and it fails when counting is switched back to the projected rows.\n"
  "2026-11-08T03:55:10.952Z","harness:claude-code","CodeRabbit review of 54e09e050, findings for this item. The CLI regression spec now decodes the TOON next_cursor, checks that its direction is backward, and replays it to verify that the adjacent older page is delivered. Kept by design, with reasons on the review thread: the newest-tail behavior of --output-limit is the intended pm-8s53lj change, aligned with the producer's own latest-N --limit, and it is declared with a before/after/migrate line in the SDK surface acknowledgment and on pm-gh1657. The MCP 20-row producer page cannot be continued by a universal output cursor, so that case is filed as pm-sbqn4h.\n"
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-08T00:39:16.886Z","harness:claude-code","A universal compaction that always keeps the first rows silently inverts the meaning of a chronological collection: for an append-only log, the head is the least useful part, and the producer's own latest-N limit already disagreed with it. Declare retention per row path as data (PM_READ_OUTPUT_TAIL_RETENTION_POLICIES), make the continuation cursor carry its direction, and refuse a cursor whose direction disagrees with the path's declaration, so pages from the two directions can never be mixed."
